**Jira card:** JUJU-4401

In Livewire components, the state is not in $_REQUEST, but directly in the class parameters. Therefore, I suggest adding an additional argument to scope filter and sort to pass the filter state.

usage example
```blade
<!-- in blade template -->

<input type="text" wire:model.live="filters.id.$eq" placeholder="user id" />
```

```php
// in livewire component class
<?php

namespace App\Livewire;

use Livewire\Component;
use App\Models\RewardPointTransaction;
use Livewire\WithPagination;
use Livewire\Attributes\Url;

class RewardPointTransacrionTable extends Component
{
    use WithPagination;

    #[Url]
    public $filters = [
        'id' => [],
    ];

    public function render()
    {
        $transactions = RewardPointTransaction::filter(null, $this->filters)->paginate(10);
        return view('livewire.reward-point-transacrion-table',compact('transactions'));
    }
}
```
